__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
arbiter-out/
arbiter-ab/
# The result cache is a machine-local memo of a previous scan (REQ-041).
# knowledge.json beside it stays tracked: that is evidence, this is not.
**/.arbiter/cache.json
build/
dist/
# Per-run training output is regenerated every cycle and would grow the
# repository without telling a later run anything. What accumulates stays:
# WORKLIST.md is the nightly handoff to whoever does the judging, and the two
# JSON files are evidence gathered over time rather than one run's logs.
#
# The directory itself must not be ignored. `training/` matched the directory,
# so the nightly job's `git add -A .arbiter training` exited 1 and threw away
# 55 minutes of measurement before it could be committed.
training/*
!training/.gitkeep
!training/WORKLIST.md
!training/fix-pairs.json
!training/disagreements.json

# Claude Code local state: settings with machine-specific paths, and the
# Headroom marker files. All of it is per-machine and none of it describes the
# project, so the directory stays out -- except settings.json, which holds the
# shared Stop hook `omni hook install` writes (`omni gate --hook`) and nothing
# machine-specific; the Headroom wiring lives in settings.local.json.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/skills/

# Same reasoning as .claude/ above, for Codex CLI: local Headroom wiring with
# a machine-specific path and profile id, not project configuration.
.codex/

# hypothesis writes an example database here: inputs that have failed before,
# replayed first on the next run. It is a local cache keyed to this machine's
# runs, and committing it would replay one developer's failures for everyone.
.hypothesis/

# OmniEngineering code graph: regenerated by `omni graph build` (and by the
# post-commit hook in .githooks/), so it is never more than one commit stale
# and never worth committing. The log and lock are the hook's scratch state.
.ai/project-graph.json
.ai/project-graph.svg
.ai/project-graph.html
.ai/.graph-build.log
.ai/.graph-build.lock/

# A per-checkout virtualenv (pip install -e . into it so a worktree tests its
# own code rather than whichever checkout is installed globally).
.venv/
